{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לתת להם את ארץ כנען", :translit "latet lahem et eretz k'na'an", :gloss "to give them the land of Canaan"} {:he "לתת עולה", :translit "latet olah", :gloss "to give elevation offering"} {:he "ת\"י ת\"ך", :translit "taf yud taf kuf", :gloss "410 420"} {:he "שנ", :translit "shin nun", :gloss "years"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לתת עולה", :b "ת\"י ת\"ך"}], :frame {:text "The First Temple stood for 410 years and the Second Temple for 420 years, as recorded in rabbinic chronology (Seder Olam Rabbah 29; Yoma 54a in reference to the First Temple's destruction calculations). The Ba'al HaTurim reads this well-known chronology into the gematria of the phrase 'לתת עולה' from the adjacent verse (Exodus 6:5), connecting the land of Canaan's gift to the Temples that would stand there.", :sources ["Seder Olam Rabbah 29" "Yoma 54a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אשר גרו בה", :translit "asher garu bah", :gloss "in which they sojourned"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Interprets the phrase 'אשר גרו בה' as referring to the ten tribes dwelling in the land."}], :frame {:text "The verse states that the patriarchs sojourned in the land of Canaan (Exodus 6:4). The Ba'al HaTurim extends the scope of 'אשר גרו בה' to address the ten northern tribes who would later dwell in that same land of Canaan before the exile of the northern kingdom by Assyria (II Kings 17:6).", :sources ["Exodus 6:4" "II Kings 17:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "לתת עולה", :a-value 941, :b "ת\"י ת\"ך", :b-value 830, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Interprets the phrase 'אשר גרו בה' as referring to the ten tribes dwelling in the land.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:14:00.192249362Z", :model "glm-5.2"}